{
  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "The evidence strongly points to scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l as the optimal modality pair (0.725 accuracy with transformer+weighted, 0.721 with transformer+concat), far outperforming pca_n2000 (~0.60) and scgpt (~0.49). The only untested variation within this winning pair is the aggregation method. config_049 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) directly tests whether the transformer aggregation is necessary for the high accuracy or whether a simpler average-pooling aggregation can match it. This is important because: (1) if avgpool performs comparably (~0.72), we identify a cheaper, simpler architecture for deployment; (2) if avgpool is clearly worse, we confirm transformer aggregation is the critical component and can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning within the transformer family. Expected cost is moderate-to-low (~3–4 GPU hours), comparable to or slightly below the transformer-based configs (3.6–4.7 GPU hours), since avgpool replaces the transformer's self-attention layers. With 2 experiments remaining, this is the highest-information test that either confirms or challenges the current best configuration's architecture."
}

